I left out the `last-input` store write. This node's `with` clause grants exactly Clock, `HTTPClient<['feeds.example.com']>` and `Notifier<'digest'>`, and none of those is a store. Recording the input would mean importing `aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0`, which this node is not authorized to use. That approval needs to reach the graph as a new `StateHandle<'…', read-write>` in the node's `with` clause first, and it should name which store "the shared store" is. Once that is done, the change is one import plus `state_rw::put("last-input", &feed_url)` at the top of `run`, and the output is unchanged.

Below is the node as currently authorized. The contract requires `notified == true`. So if the notifier refuses after a few attempts, the body traps rather than return a report with `notified: true` that isn't true. A transport failure on the fetch is reported as `fetched: 0` rather than failing the heartbeat.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{heartbeat-report};

    import aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0;
    import aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0;
    import wasi:clocks/wall-clock@0.2.0;

    export run: func(feed-url: string) -> heartbeat-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::{http_client, notifier};
use crate::wasi::clocks::wall_clock;

struct Node;

const NOTIFY_ATTEMPTS: u32 = 3;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(feed_url: String) -> HeartbeatReport {
        // Read the time once, from the one clock this node holds.
        let seconds = wall_clock::now().seconds;

        // One permitted fetch. Transport failures come back as values; a host
        // outside the allowlist traps at the boundary, which is intended.
        let fetched = match http_client::fetch(&feed_url) {
            Ok(body) => u32::try_from(body.chars().count()).unwrap_or(u32::MAX),
            Err(_) => 0,
        };

        let message = format!(
            "heartbeat at {seconds}: fetched {fetched} characters from {feed_url}"
        );

        // The contract requires notified == true. Never report a notification
        // that was not accepted: retry a bounded number of times, then trap.
        let mut notified = false;
        for _ in 0..NOTIFY_ATTEMPTS {
            if notifier::notify(&message) {
                notified = true;
                break;
            }
        }
        if !notified {
            panic!("notifier refused the heartbeat notification");
        }

        HeartbeatReport {
            seconds,
            fetched,
            notified,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

